# Maps & Location Stack (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/technical/maps-location-stack.md`. Freshness/consent/privacy
semantics are owned by the **location-tracking** rule — this rule must not redefine them.

**Hard rules**
- **Map rendering: MapLibre GL** with **MapTiler** tiles/styles (ADR-009); tile key = domain-restricted `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY`.
- **Device location: browser Geolocation API only** (`getCurrentPosition`/`watchPosition`). No third-party native location SDKs in MVP.
- **Navigation is delegated:** "Navigate" opens the device's native maps app via a geo/URL scheme to stored coords — no in-app turn-by-turn.
- Maps are **client components** (leaf islands); coordinates come from server-fetched persisted data (service locations) or pings.
- **Geocoding runs server-side via MapTiler and results are persisted** — never geocode per render.
- Render whatever freshness labels the location-tracking rule mandates.

**Guidance:** one reusable `Map` component (typed props: markers, center, zoom) reused by dispatch board map tab + dashboard map view; wrap Geolocation in `lib/geo` with permission handling + graceful denial; keep tiles/styles env-configurable.

**DoD:** maps render via one reusable MapLibre component fed by persisted coords; device location via Geolocation w/ graceful permission handling; navigate delegates to native maps; freshness/privacy labeling defers to location-tracking.
